<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>That's the body of my problem. What this was <em>supposed</em> to be, is a Deep State version of the Foundation. They hid the documentation within the normal listings (Plain Sight) and they've been designing this organism and infecting the world with it. I don't know how it would be possible to state that without actually stating that, which would defeat the point of them operating in secrecy.</p>
<p>The &quot;puzzle&quot; isn't so much about that, as it is just simply that it's old Dr. Kondraki in charge of this program now, and he's plotting (successfully, at this point) to take over not just the Foundation, but the world itself, by using this to make people produce butterfly pheromones. But honestly, I didn't care if that part came through to everyone - that was just an Easter Egg for the hell of it. The main point was supposed to be the above paragraph. There's no anomaly here, there's nothing weird going on at all, except that a bunch of scientists are intentionally fucking up human biology for the sake of their version of the &quot;greater good.&quot; Since this is inevitably going to fail, I'll stick it back in my sandbox when it does and pull it back later if I can figure out a way to rework it so the &quot;Deep State&quot; bit is more obvious. I just feel like, by doing so, it kind of makes it not a &quot;Deep State&quot; and thus less intrinsically sinister.</p>
